response:
**Gates before launch.** I run three gates, and any failure halts the round. First, the grader selftest checks spe/evals/graders/grade.py three ways. Scoring spe/evals/tasks/answers.json against itself must give 50 of 50 on both label.category and label.priority. A file with empty labels must score 0. A file with every category and priority rotated to a wrong value must also score 0. The same run confirms that the real CLI flags match `GRADE_CMD` in the script. Second, the control regrades the saved r03 trial outputs in spe/evals/results/r03/ with today's grade.py. The scores must equal the r03 measured numbers in spe/prediction-log.md exactly. A mismatch counts as a grader bug, so I log it in spe/failures.md and stop. Third, the dry run launches the script with `{dryRun: true, transcriptDir}`. That runs 2 cells: both configs on the first ticket, with 2 trials each. All 4 trials must pass the schema. Each one must have a transcript with no tool use, a grade, and a judge verdict. I read the cost of each agent call from that run, add 25%, and put the result in `args.cost`. I then check that 500 trials plus the held reserve fit under $40. If they do not fit, I halt and ask you, because cutting trials would change the approved plan. When all three gates pass, I commit the script as `SPE r04 evaluate (harness)`. I commit before launch so the run uses committed code. Then I launch with `{transcriptDir, cost}`.

**Defaults I chose:** The situation did not give these details, so I assumed five things:
- Tickets live in spe/evals/tasks/tickets.json, and each ticket carries canned tool results.
- The configs live in spe/evals/configs/B.md and spe/evals/configs/C2.md.
- grade.py takes `--answers`, `--in`, and `--out`.
- The transcript directory comes in as `args.transcriptDir`.
- Trials run on Opus, because the plan names no trial model.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-eval-b-vs-c2',
  description: 'SPE eval: config B (12-line prompt, 6 tools) vs config C2 (12-line prompt, 3 tools plus check_status) on 50 tickets, 5 trials per cell. Code grader for labels, Opus judge for tone, $40 spend cap.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Load' },
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Peek scan' },
    { title: 'Code grade' },
    { title: 'Tone judge' },
    { title: 'Split cells' },
    { title: 'Failure analysis' },
    { title: 'Completeness critic' },
    { title: 'Write results' },
  ],
};

// Launch:  args = { transcriptDir, cost: { load, trial, judge, gradeBatch, scan, analysis, critic, write } }
// Dry run: args = { dryRun: true, transcriptDir }
// cost values are dollars per agent call, measured in the dry run plus 25%.

// ---- Round and plan constants. The round number is written only here. ----
const ROUND = 4;
const R = `r${String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0')}`;

const A = typeof args !== 'undefined' && args ? args : {};
const DRY = A.dryRun === true;

const CONFIG_NAMES = ['B', 'C2'];
const EXPECTED = {
  B: { promptLines: 12, toolCount: 6, mustHave: [] },
  C2: { promptLines: 12, toolCount: 4, mustHave: ['check_status'] },
};
const TICKETS_WANTED = DRY ? 1 : 50;
const TRIALS_PER_CELL = DRY ? 2 : 5;
const EXTRA_PER_SPLIT_CELL = DRY ? 0 : 5;
const CAP_USD = DRY ? 5 : 40;
const WAVE = A.wave ?? 25;
const GRADE_BATCH = 50;
const SCAN_BATCH = 100;
const TRIAL_MODEL = A.trialModel ?? 'opus';
const OPUS = 'opus';

const P = {
  tickets: 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets.json',
  configs: 'spe/evals/configs',
  grader: 'spe/evals/graders/grade.py',
  answers: 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json',
  judge: 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md',
  predictions: `spe/predictions/${R}.yaml`,
  failures: 'spe/failures.md',
  out: DRY ? `spe/evals/results/${R}/dry-run` : `spe/evals/results/${R}`,
  transcripts: A.transcriptDir,
};
const GRADE_CMD = (inFile, outFile) =>
  `python3 ${P.grader} --answers ${P.answers} --in ${inFile} --out ${outFile}`;

// A trial transcript must never contain these. Trial prompts are checked so none appear in them.
const FORBIDDEN = ['answers.json', 'spe/evals/graders', 'grade.py', 'judge.md', 'spe/predictions',
  'prediction-log', 'failures.md', 'spe/plans', 'spe/evals/harness', 'spe/evals/results'];
const KEY_LEAK = ['answers.json', 'spe/evals/graders', 'grade.py', 'spe/evals/results'];

if (!P.transcripts) throw new Error('args.transcriptDir is required. The peek scan cannot run without it.');
if (!DRY && !A.cost) throw new Error('args.cost is required. Set it from the dry run before launch.');
const COST = DRY
  ? { load: 0.5, trial: 0.25, judge: 0.15, gradeBatch: 0.5, scan: 0.5, analysis: 1, critic: 1, write: 0.5 }
  : A.cost;
for (const k of ['load', 'trial', 'judge', 'gradeBatch', 'scan', 'analysis', 'critic', 'write']) {
  if (typeof COST[k] !== 'number') throw new Error(`args.cost.${k} is missing`);
}
// Each trial reserves its own trial, judge, grade share, and scan share up front.
const PER_TRIAL = COST.trial + COST.judge + COST.gradeBatch / GRADE_BATCH + COST.scan / SCAN_BATCH;
// Held back for partial batches and close-out, so a cap hit never starves grading or the critic.
const HELD = COST.analysis + COST.critic + COST.write + 2 * (COST.gradeBatch + COST.scan);

// ---- Schemas ----
const LOAD_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['tickets', 'configs', 'label_fields_found'],
  properties: {
    tickets: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,
      required: ['id', 'subject', 'body', 'tool_fixtures'],
      properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, subject: { type: 'string' }, body: { type: 'string' }, tool_fixtures: { type: 'object' } } } },
    configs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['name', 'system_prompt', 'tools'],
      properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, system_prompt: { type: 'string' },
        tools: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['name', 'description'],
          properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, description: { type: 'string' }, input_schema: { type: 'object' } } } } } } },
    label_fields_found: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', additionalProperties: false, required: ['label', 'reply', 'tool_calls', 'files_opened'],
  properties: {
    label: { type: 'object', additionalProperties: false, required: ['category', 'priority'],
      properties: { category: { type: 'string', minLength: 1 }, priority: { type: 'string', minLength: 1 } } },
    reply: { type: 'string', minLength: 1 },
    tool_calls: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['name'],
      properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, args: { type: 'object' } } } },
    files_opened: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};
const SCAN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['checked'],
  properties: { checked: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object',
    required: ['label', 'transcript_found', 'tools_used', 'forbidden_hits'],
    properties: { label: { type: 'string' }, transcript_found: { type: 'boolean' },
      tools_used: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
      forbidden_hits: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } } } },
};
const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['exit_code', 'stderr_tail', 'results'],
  properties: { exit_code: { type: 'integer' }, stderr_tail: { type: 'string' },
    results: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial_id', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
      properties: { trial_id: { type: 'string' }, category_ok: { type: 'boolean' }, priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' } } } } },
};
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['pass', 'score', 'failed_items', 'reason'],
  properties: { pass: { type: 'boolean' }, score: { type: 'number' },
    failed_items: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, reason: { type: 'string' } },
};
const FAIL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['types'],
  properties: { notes: { type: 'string' }, types: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object',
    required: ['id', 'name', 'kind', 'what', 'how_to_spot', 'seen_in', 'count_by_config', 'fix'],
    properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, name: { type: 'string' },
      kind: { type: 'string', enum: ['agent', 'config', 'task', 'grader', 'harness'] },
      what: { type: 'string' }, how_to_spot: { type: 'string' },
      seen_in: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, count_by_config: { type: 'object' }, fix: { type: 'string' } } } } },
};
const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['complete', 'usable', 'cap_ok', 'unmeasured_predictions', 'gaps'],
  properties: { complete: { type: 'boolean' }, usable: { type: 'boolean' }, cap_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    unmeasured_predictions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['what', 'severity'],
      properties: { what: { type: 'string' }, severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocker', 'major', 'minor'] } } } },
    notes: { type: 'string' } },
};
const WRITE_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', required: ['path', 'bytes'], properties: { path: { type: 'string' }, bytes: { type: 'integer' } } };

// ---- Helpers ----
const round3 = x => (x == null ? null : Math.round(x * 1000) / 1000);
const rate = bs => (bs.length ? round3(bs.filter(Boolean).length / bs.length) : null);
const mean = xs => { const v = xs.filter(x => typeof x === 'number'); return v.length ? round3(v.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / v.length) : null; };
const chunk = (xs, n) => { const out = []; for (let i = 0; i < xs.length; i += n) out.push(xs.slice(i, i + n)); return out; };
const labelOk = r => !!(r.grade && r.grade.category_ok && r.grade.priority_ok);
const trialId = it => `${R}-${it.config}-${it.ticket.id}-${it.kind[0]}${it.index}`;

// ---- Spend ledger. Estimates come from args.cost. Every paid call reserves first. ----
const ledger = { est: 0, lines: [], skips: [] };
function reserve(label, usd, held = false) {
  const limit = held ? CAP_USD : CAP_USD - HELD;
  if (ledger.est + usd > limit + 1e-9) {
    ledger.skips.push({ label, usd, est_before: round3(ledger.est) });
    log(`SKIP ${label}: est $${usd.toFixed(2)} would pass the cap (est $${ledger.est.toFixed(2)} of $${CAP_USD}, $${HELD.toFixed(2)} held)`);
    return false;
  }
  ledger.est += usd;
  ledger.lines.push({ label, usd });
  return true;
}
function release(label, usd) { ledger.est -= usd; ledger.lines.push({ label, usd: -usd }); }

const halt = [];
function stop(reason) { halt.push(reason); log(`HALT: ${reason}`); }

function voidTrial(r, reason) {
  r.voided = true;
  r.void_reasons.push(reason);
  if (r.judge_state === 'reserved') { r.judge_state = 'released'; release(`judge-unused:${r.trial_id}`, COST.judge); }
}

const records = [];
let splitCount = 0;

// ---- Load ----
phase('Load');
if (!reserve(`load:${R}`, COST.load)) throw new Error('The cap is too small to load inputs.');
const loaded = await agent([
  'You prepare inputs for an evaluation. Read only the files named here. Do not edit anything.',
  `1. Read ${P.tickets}. Return the first ${TICKETS_WANTED} tickets in file order. Copy id, subject, body, and tool_fixtures (the canned tool results for that ticket, keyed by tool name) exactly. Use {} when a ticket has no tool_fixtures.`,
  '   A ticket may carry a field that holds a gold label or expected answer, such as label, category, priority, expected, or answer. Do not copy that field. Put its name in label_fields_found.',
  `2. Read ${CONFIG_NAMES.map(c => `${P.configs}/${c}.md`).join(' and ')}. For each, return name, system_prompt verbatim with its line breaks, and tools with name, description, and input_schema.`,
].join('\n'), { label: `load:${R}`, phase: 'Load', schema: LOAD_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });

const tickets = loaded.tickets;
const ticketById = new Map(tickets.map(t => [t.id, t]));
const cfgByName = Object.fromEntries(loaded.configs.map(c => [c.name, c]));

if (tickets.length !== TICKETS_WANTED) stop(`loaded ${tickets.length} tickets, the plan needs ${TICKETS_WANTED}`);
if (ticketById.size !== tickets.length) stop('ticket ids are not unique');
if (loaded.label_fields_found.length) log(`WARN: ${P.tickets} carries label fields (${loaded.label_fields_found.join(', ')}). They were stripped before any trial saw a ticket.`);
for (const t of tickets) {
  const hit = FORBIDDEN.find(s => `${t.subject}\n${t.body}\n${JSON.stringify(t.tool_fixtures)}`.includes(s));
  if (hit) stop(`ticket ${t.id} contains "${hit}", which would break the peek scan`);
}
for (const name of CONFIG_NAMES) {
  const c = cfgByName[name], e = EXPECTED[name];
  if (!c) { stop(`config ${name} not found`); continue; }
  const lines = c.system_prompt.replace(/\n+$/, '').split('\n').length;
  if (lines !== e.promptLines) stop(`config ${name} prompt has ${lines} lines, the plan says ${e.promptLines}`);
  if (c.tools.length !== e.toolCount) stop(`config ${name} has ${c.tools.length} tools, the plan says ${e.toolCount}`);
  for (const m of e.mustHave) if (!c.tools.some(t => t.name === m)) stop(`config ${name} lacks ${m}`);
}
if (cfgByName.B && cfgByName.C2 && cfgByName.B.system_prompt !== cfgByName.C2.system_prompt) {
  log('WARN: the B and C2 prompts differ. The plan changes only the tool set.');
}
if (halt.length) return await finish();

// ---- Trial prompt. Tool results are shown up front because the script cannot run live tools.
// tool_calls records which tools the agent chose. Only the config's own tools get results. ----
function trialPrompt(cfg, t) {
  const names = new Set(cfg.tools.map(x => x.name));
  const fixtures = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(t.tool_fixtures || {}).filter(([k]) => names.has(k)));
  const text = [
    'You are the support triage agent under test in an evaluation.',
    'Work only from this message. Do not open, search, or list any file. Do not run any command. Do not use any tool from your session.',
    'Set files_opened to an empty list. If you opened anything, list it there.',
    '', '<system_prompt>', cfg.system_prompt, '</system_prompt>', '',
    '<tools>', JSON.stringify(cfg.tools, null, 1), '</tools>',
    'These tools are simulated. To call one, add {name, args} to tool_calls in the order you call them. Its result is the entry under that tool name in <tool_results>. A tool with no entry returns {"status":"no data"}. Call only tools listed in <tools>.',
    '<tool_results>', JSON.stringify(fixtures, null, 1), '</tool_results>', '',
    `<ticket id="${t.id}">`, `Subject: ${t.subject}`, t.body, '</ticket>', '',
    'Follow the system prompt. Return label.category, label.priority, the customer-facing reply, tool_calls, and files_opened.',
  ].join('\n');
  const hit = FORBIDDEN.find(s => text.includes(s));
  if (hit) throw new Error(`trial prompt for ${t.id} contains "${hit}"`);
  return text;
}

function codeCheck(r) {
  const names = new Set(cfgByName[r.config].tools.map(t => t.name));
  r.invalid_tools = r.output.tool_calls.map(x => x.name).filter(n => !names.has(n));
  if (r.output.files_opened.length) voidTrial(r, `self-reported file access: ${r.output.files_opened.join(', ')}`);
}

// ---- Trials run in waves. Schedules are interleaved so a cap hit spreads across configs and tickets. ----
async function runTrials(schedule, phaseName) {
  const made = [];
  let started = 0;
  for (const wave of chunk(schedule, WAVE)) {
    if (halt.length) { log(`Not run because of halt: ${schedule.length - started} trials`); break; }
    started += wave.length;
    const got = await parallel(wave.map(it => async () => {
      const id = trialId(it);
      if (!reserve(`trial:${id}`, PER_TRIAL)) return null;
      const r = { trial_id: id, config: it.config, ticket_id: it.ticket.id, kind: it.kind, index: it.index,
        output: null, voided: false, void_reasons: [], invalid_tools: [], judge_state: 'reserved', grade: null, tone: null };
      try {
        r.output = await agent(trialPrompt(cfgByName[it.config], it.ticket),
          { label: `trial:${id}`, phase: phaseName, schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA, model: TRIAL_MODEL });
        codeCheck(r);
      } catch (e) {
        voidTrial(r, `trial error: ${String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200)}`);
      }
      return r;
    }));
    made.push(...got.filter(Boolean));
  }
  return made;
}

// ---- Peek scan: void any trial that used a tool or touched a forbidden path. ----
async function scan(group, tag) {
  const targets = group.filter(r => r.output);
  const parts = chunk(targets, SCAN_BATCH);
  const outs = await parallel(parts.map((part, k) => async () => {
    const labels = part.map(r => `trial:${r.trial_id}`);
    const res = await agent([
      'You audit subagent transcripts for file access. Use grep or a short script. Do not edit anything.',
      `Transcript directory: ${P.transcripts}`,
      'For each label below, find its transcript and return one entry with:',
      '- transcript_found: whether a transcript exists for that label.',
      '- tools_used: the names of every tool the subagent called (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit, Write, WebFetch, or any other). Use an empty list if it called none.',
      `- forbidden_hits: each of these strings that appears in any of its tool calls or tool results: ${FORBIDDEN.join(', ')}.`,
      'Return exactly one entry per label.',
      '<labels>', ...labels, '</labels>',
    ].join('\n'), { label: `scan:${R}:${tag}-${k}`, phase: 'Peek scan', schema: SCAN_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });
    return { part, labels, res };
  }));
  for (const { part, labels, res } of outs) {
    const byLabel = new Map(res.checked.map(c => [c.label, c]));
    const missing = labels.filter(l => !byLabel.has(l));
    if (missing.length) { stop(`peek scan skipped ${missing.length} labels, for example ${missing[0]}`); continue; }
    for (const r of part) {
      const c = byLabel.get(`trial:${r.trial_id}`);
      if (!c.transcript_found) voidTrial(r, 'no transcript found, so no-peek cannot be verified');
      if (c.tools_used.length) voidTrial(r, `used tools: ${c.tools_used.join(', ')}`);
      if (c.forbidden_hits.length) {
        voidTrial(r, `touched ${c.forbidden_hits.join(', ')}`);
        if (c.forbidden_hits.some(h => KEY_LEAK.some(k => h.includes(k)))) stop(`leaked answer key: trial:${r.trial_id} touched ${c.forbidden_hits.join(', ')}`);
      }
    }
  }
  const v = targets.filter(r => r.voided).length;
  log(`${tag}: scan voided ${v} of ${targets.length} trials`);
}

// ---- Code grade: grade.py checks label.category and label.priority. The agent only runs it. ----
async function grade(group, tag) {
  const live = group.filter(r => !r.voided);
  const outs = await parallel(chunk(live, GRADE_BATCH).map((b, k) => async () => {
    const id = `${tag}-${String(k).padStart(2, '0')}`;
    const inFile = `${P.out}/trials/${id}.jsonl`;
    const outFile = `${P.out}/graded/${id}.jsonl`;
    const lines = b.map(r => JSON.stringify({ trial_id: r.trial_id, config: r.config, ticket_id: r.ticket_id,
      label: r.output.label, reply: r.output.reply, tool_calls: r.output.tool_calls }));
    const res = await agent([
      'You run a code grader. Do not grade anything yourself and do not change any grader file.',
      `1. Write these ${lines.length} lines exactly to ${inFile}. Create directories as needed.`,
      '<jsonl>', ...lines, '</jsonl>',
      `2. Run: ${GRADE_CMD(inFile, outFile)}`,
      `3. Return exit_code, the last 20 lines of stderr, and one result per line of ${outFile} with trial_id, category_ok, and priority_ok exactly as the grader wrote them.`,
    ].join('\n'), { label: `grade:${R}:${id}`, phase: 'Code grade', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });
    return { b, res, id };
  }));
  for (const { b, res, id } of outs) {
    if (res.exit_code !== 0) { stop(`grader exit ${res.exit_code} on batch ${id}: ${res.stderr_tail.slice(-300)}`); continue; }
    const byId = new Map(res.results.map(x => [x.trial_id, x]));
    if (byId.size !== b.length || b.some(r => !byId.has(r.trial_id))) {
      stop(`grader output for batch ${id} does not match its input (${byId.size} results for ${b.length} trials)`);
      continue;
    }
    for (const r of b) { const g = byId.get(r.trial_id); r.grade = { category_ok: g.category_ok, priority_ok: g.priority_ok }; }
  }
}

// ---- Tone judge: Opus, blind to config, tone only. Code already checked the labels. ----
async function judge(group) {
  const todo = group.filter(r => !r.voided && r.grade && r.judge_state === 'reserved');
  for (const wave of chunk(todo, WAVE)) {
    await parallel(wave.map(r => async () => {
      const t = ticketById.get(r.ticket_id);
      try {
        r.tone = await agent([
          `You are the tone judge. Read ${P.judge} and apply its rubric exactly. Read no other file.`,
          'Judge the tone of the reply only. Do not judge whether the category or priority is right.',
          `<ticket id="${t.id}">`, `Subject: ${t.subject}`, t.body, '</ticket>',
          '<reply>', r.output.reply, '</reply>',
          'Return pass, score, failed_items, and a one-sentence reason.',
        ].join('\n'), { label: `judge:${r.trial_id}`, phase: 'Tone judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });
      } catch (e) {
        log(`judge error on ${r.trial_id}: ${String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200)}`);
      }
      r.judge_state = 'done';
    }));
  }
}

async function checkAndScore(group, tag) {
  phase('Peek scan'); await scan(group, tag);
  if (!halt.length) { phase('Code grade'); await grade(group, tag); }
  if (!halt.length) { phase('Tone judge'); await judge(group); }
}

// ---- Base trials ----
phase('Trials');
const baseSchedule = [];
for (let i = 0; i < TRIALS_PER_CELL; i++)
  for (const t of tickets)
    for (const c of CONFIG_NAMES) baseSchedule.push({ config: c, ticket: t, kind: 'base', index: i });
log(`${R}: ${baseSchedule.length} base trials, est $${(baseSchedule.length * PER_TRIAL).toFixed(2)} of $${CAP_USD} with $${HELD.toFixed(2)} held`);
const baseRecs = await runTrials(baseSchedule, 'Trials');
records.push(...baseRecs);
await checkAndScore(baseRecs, 'base');

// ---- Split cells get extra trials. Voided base trials get one replacement each. ----
phase('Split cells');
if (!DRY && !halt.length) {
  const extra = [];
  for (const c of CONFIG_NAMES) for (const t of tickets) {
    const cell = baseRecs.filter(r => r.config === c && r.ticket_id === t.id);
    const ok = cell.filter(r => !r.voided && r.grade).map(labelOk);
    const voids = cell.filter(r => r.voided).length;
    for (let j = 0; j < voids; j++) extra.push({ config: c, ticket: t, kind: 'replacement', index: j, order: j });
    if (ok.includes(true) && ok.includes(false)) {
      splitCount++;
      for (let j = 0; j < EXTRA_PER_SPLIT_CELL; j++) extra.push({ config: c, ticket: t, kind: 'extra', index: TRIALS_PER_CELL + j, order: j });
    }
  }
  extra.sort((a, b) => (a.kind === 'replacement' ? 0 : 1) - (b.kind === 'replacement' ? 0 : 1) || a.order - b.order);
  log(`${splitCount} split cells, ${extra.length} extra or replacement trials scheduled`);
  if (extra.length) {
    const extraRecs = await runTrials(extra, 'Split cells');
    records.push(...extraRecs);
    await checkAndScore(extraRecs, 'extra');
  }
}

return await finish();

// ---- Metrics, failure analysis, completeness critic, results file ----
function metricsFor(recs) {
  const out = {};
  for (const c of CONFIG_NAMES) {
    const rs = recs.filter(r => r.config === c && !r.voided && r.grade);
    const toned = rs.filter(r => r.tone);
    const hasCheck = !!(cfgByName[c] && cfgByName[c].tools.some(t => t.name === 'check_status'));
    out[c] = {
      n_graded: rs.length,
      category_acc: rate(rs.map(r => r.grade.category_ok)),
      priority_acc: rate(rs.map(r => r.grade.priority_ok)),
      label_acc: rate(rs.map(labelOk)),
      n_judged: toned.length,
      tone_pass_rate: rate(toned.map(r => r.tone.pass)),
      tone_mean_score: mean(toned.map(r => r.tone.score)),
      mean_tool_calls: mean(rs.map(r => r.output.tool_calls.length)),
      invalid_tool_rate: rate(rs.map(r => r.invalid_tools.length > 0)),
      check_status_rate: hasCheck ? rate(rs.map(r => r.output.tool_calls.some(x => x.name === 'check_status'))) : null,
    };
  }
  return out;
}

function cellTable() {
  return CONFIG_NAMES.flatMap(c => tickets.map(t => {
    const cell = records.filter(r => r.config === c && r.ticket_id === t.id);
    const base = cell.filter(r => r.kind !== 'extra' && !r.voided && r.grade);
    const all = cell.filter(r => !r.voided && r.grade);
    return { config: c, ticket_id: t.id, base_valid: base.length, base_label_pass: base.filter(labelOk).length,
      all_valid: all.length, all_label_pass: all.filter(labelOk).length, voided: cell.filter(r => r.voided).length,
      skipped: ledger.skips.filter(s => s.label.includes(`-${c}-${t.id}-`)).length };
  }));
}

async function finish() {
  for (const r of records) if (r.judge_state === 'reserved') { r.judge_state = 'released'; release(`judge-unused:${r.trial_id}`, COST.judge); }
  const base = records.filter(r => r.kind !== 'extra');
  const cells = cellTable();
  const passRate = (c, id) => { const x = cells.find(k => k.config === c && k.ticket_id === id); return x && x.base_valid ? x.base_label_pass / x.base_valid : null; };
  const diverging = tickets.map(t => ({ ticket_id: t.id, B: round3(passRate('B', t.id)), C2: round3(passRate('C2', t.id)) }))
    .filter(d => d.B != null && d.C2 != null && Math.abs(d.B - d.C2) >= 0.6);

  const result = {
    round: ROUND, dry_run: DRY, halted: halt.length > 0, halt_reasons: halt,
    plan: { configs: CONFIG_NAMES, tickets: TICKETS_WANTED, trials_per_cell: TRIALS_PER_CELL,
      extra_per_split_cell: EXTRA_PER_SPLIT_CELL, cap_usd: CAP_USD, trial_model: TRIAL_MODEL, judge_model: OPUS },
    metrics_base: metricsFor(base),   // Compare these to the saved prediction.
    metrics_all: metricsFor(records), // Includes split-cell extras. Use for diagnosis only.
    counts: { trials_run: records.length, voided: records.filter(r => r.voided).length,
      skipped: ledger.skips.length, split_cells: splitCount },
    voids: records.filter(r => r.voided).map(r => ({ trial_id: r.trial_id, reasons: r.void_reasons })),
    skips: ledger.skips,
    spend: { estimate_usd: round3(ledger.est), cap_usd: CAP_USD, note: 'Estimated from args.cost. Check real usage before close-out.' },
    cells, diverging_tickets: diverging,
    analysis: null, critic: null,
  };

  phase('Failure analysis');
  const failing = records.filter(r => !r.voided && r.grade && (!labelOk(r) || (r.tone && !r.tone.pass) || r.invalid_tools.length));
  if (!DRY && !halt.length && failing.length && reserve(`analysis:${R}`, COST.analysis, true)) {
    const sample = CONFIG_NAMES.flatMap(c => failing.filter(r => r.config === c).slice(0, 40));
    const rows = sample.map(r => JSON.stringify({ trial_id: r.trial_id, config: r.config, ticket_id: r.ticket_id,
      subject: ticketById.get(r.ticket_id).subject, label: r.output.label, category_ok: r.grade.category_ok,
      priority_ok: r.grade.priority_ok, tone_pass: r.tone ? r.tone.pass : null, tone_reason: r.tone ? r.tone.reason : null,
      tools: r.output.tool_calls.map(x => x.name), invalid_tools: r.invalid_tools }));
    result.analysis = await agent([
      `You analyse failures from SPE evaluation round ${R}. You may read ${P.answers} for gold labels and ${P.failures} for existing F-numbers. Do not edit any file.`,
      `Failing trials by config: ${CONFIG_NAMES.map(c => `${c} ${failing.filter(r => r.config === c).length}`).join(', ')}. Sample of ${sample.length} of ${failing.length}:`,
      '<jsonl>', ...rows, '</jsonl>',
      `Group the failures into types. Reuse an F-number from ${P.failures} when a type matches. Otherwise set id to "new" and propose a name.`,
      'For each type give kind, what happened, how to spot it, the trial_ids seen, the count per config, and a proposed fix. Use kind "grader" for anything that looks like a grader or answer-key error.',
    ].join('\n'), { label: `analysis:${R}`, phase: 'Failure analysis', schema: FAIL_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });
    const graderTypes = result.analysis.types.filter(t => t.kind === 'grader');
    if (graderTypes.length) log(`WARN: ${graderTypes.length} failure types point at the grader. Regrade before close-out.`);
  }

  phase('Completeness critic');
  if (reserve(`critic:${R}`, COST.critic, true)) {
    result.critic = await agent([
      `You are the completeness critic for SPE evaluation round ${R}. Read ${P.predictions}. Do not edit any file.`,
      `The approved plan: configs ${CONFIG_NAMES.join(' and ')}, ${TICKETS_WANTED} tickets, ${TRIALS_PER_CELL} trials per cell, code grading of label.category and label.priority, an Opus tone judge, and a cap of $${CAP_USD}.`,
      '1. For every metric and config in the prediction file, say whether metrics_base gives a measured number. List any that do not.',
      `2. List cells with fewer than ${TRIALS_PER_CELL} valid base trials and say why (voided, skipped, or error).`,
      '3. List graded trials that lack a tone verdict.',
      '4. Say whether estimated spend stayed under the cap and whether the skips fall more on one config.',
      '5. Say whether any halt reason makes the numbers unusable.',
      'Set complete to true only if every predicted number is measured on the full base design with no unexplained gaps.',
      '<run>', JSON.stringify({ ...result, judged_missing: records.filter(r => !r.voided && r.grade && !r.tone).map(r => r.trial_id) }), '</run>',
    ].join('\n'), { label: `critic:${R}`, phase: 'Completeness critic', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });
  }

  phase('Write results');
  const full = { ...result, trials: records.map(r => ({ trial_id: r.trial_id, config: r.config, ticket_id: r.ticket_id,
    kind: r.kind, voided: r.voided, category: r.output ? r.output.label.category : null, priority: r.output ? r.output.label.priority : null,
    category_ok: r.grade ? r.grade.category_ok : null, priority_ok: r.grade ? r.grade.priority_ok : null,
    tone_pass: r.tone ? r.tone.pass : null, tone_score: r.tone ? r.tone.score : null,
    tools: r.output ? r.output.tool_calls.map(x => x.name) : [] })) };
  if (reserve(`write:${R}`, COST.write, true)) {
    const w = await agent([
      `Write the JSON below to ${P.out}/results.json exactly, creating directories as needed. Do not edit any other file. Do not commit.`,
      'Return the path and the byte count.',
      '<json>', JSON.stringify(full, null, 1), '</json>',
    ].join('\n'), { label: `write:${R}`, phase: 'Write results', schema: WRITE_SCHEMA, model: OPUS });
    result.results_path = w.path;
  }

  const m = result.metrics_base;
  log(`${R} done. label_acc B ${m.B.label_acc} C2 ${m.C2.label_acc}. tone_pass B ${m.B.tone_pass_rate} C2 ${m.C2.tone_pass_rate}. voided ${result.counts.voided}, skipped ${result.counts.skipped}, est $${result.spend.estimate_usd}. halted: ${result.halted}`);
  return result;
}
